{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift#L24"},"externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","title":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph stored as adjacency lists: the undirected counterpart of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacency_list<…, undirectedS>"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex set is any set of "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and "},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same edge as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each slot has a row of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash) answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-17f2v","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2o9bq","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/d